<title>HUNGARY: Croatia strike blocks rail traffic with Hungary.</title>
<headline>Croatia strike blocks rail traffic with Hungary.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 600 freight cars were held up on the Croatian-Hungarian border on Tuesday by a six-day old strike of Croatian railway workers, Hungarian Television (MTV) said.</p>
<p>Some 80 percent of Croatian rail traffic was stopped on November 28 when 11,000 HZ employees began a national strike for wage increases and better working conditions.</p>
<p>The televison said rail traffic between the two countries had almost ground to a standstill by Tuesday.</p>
<p>MTV said that only one passenger train crossed the Croatian-Hungarian border on Tuesday. It said the blockade affected 10 international passenger trains and 30 to 40 freight trains a day.</p>
</text>
